{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "id": "domashniy-arest-s01e01-scene-01",
 "pair": "ru-en",
 "title": "Подарки из Венгрии  (Gifts from Hungary)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "arkady": "Аркадий",
  "father": "Отец Самсона",
  "samson": "Самсон"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "This series is called House Arrest, and its hero is Arkady, the mayor of Sineozersk, a small Russian town; he grew up in a communal flat, one flat shared by several families. But we start in the nineteen eighties: Samson, then just little Vanya, sees his father come home from Hungary with presents, and little Arkady can only watch. Let's listen in Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Привет, папа!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "Привет! Смотри, что у меня есть.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Ого, магнитофон! Японский!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Здравствуйте! Как там в Венгрии?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "Хорошо! Там всё нормально.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Папа, а жвачку ты привёз?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "Жвачку? Денег не хватило.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Ну, папа!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "Ладно, держи. Вот, смотри.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Сколько жвачки! Класс!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "А это тебе. Машинка!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Спасибо, папа!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "Со всеми поделись поровну, понял?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Понял.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "А можно я пойду посмотрю?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Нельзя? Ладно, пойду учить уроки.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's go back through it slowly. The door bangs, and the whole corridor knows that Vanya's father is home from abroad.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Привет, папа!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Hi, Dad!' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Привет",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the casual word for hello you use with family and friends. Dad has something to show him.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "Смотри, что у меня есть.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Look what I've got.' The phrase ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "у меня есть",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally translates to 'at me there is'. That's how you say you have something. The first thing out of the suitcase is a big one.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Ого, магнитофон! Японский!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Wow, a tape recorder! A Japanese one!' the term for tape recorder, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "магнитофон",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", was a real treasure in the Soviet nineteen eighties, and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "ого",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the cry of 'wow!'. Little Arkady is watching from the doorway, and he greets the father politely.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Здравствуйте!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Hello!' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Здравствуйте",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the long, polite word for hello a child uses with a grown-up; it literally translates to wishing the other person good health. Then he asks a question a neighbour asked.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Как там в Венгрии?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'How was it there in Hungary?' Literally, translates to 'how is it there, in Hungary'. After the little word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "в",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", meaning 'in', the expression for Hungary, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Венгрии",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", shifts its last sound to ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Венгрии",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ". The father keeps it short.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "Хорошо! Там всё нормально.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Good! Everything's fine over there.' which translates to fine, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "нормально",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", sounds a lot like 'normal', and Russians use it constantly for 'fine' or 'all good'. Vanya only cares about one thing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Папа, а жвачку ты привёз?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Dad, did you bring any gum?' Russian needs no helper word like 'did' here: a rising voice turns ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "ты привёз",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " straight into a question, and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "привёз",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the action word used by a male speaker. Dad likes to tease.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "Жвачку? Денег не хватило.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Gum? I didn't have enough money.' In Russian, meaning money, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "Денег",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", is always treated like 'funds', and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "не хватило",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally translates to 'it didn't suffice'. Vanya is not having it.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Ну, папа!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Oh, come on, Dad!' The tiny word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "ну",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " at the front does all the pleading work of 'oh, come on'. So Dad gives in.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "Ладно, держи.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'All right, here you go.' the Russian word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "держи",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally translates to 'hold', and Russians say it whenever they hand something over. Then he points.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "Вот, смотри.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'There, look.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "Вот",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the pointing word Russians use as they show or hand you something, paired with the action word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "смотри",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", which translates to 'look'. Vanya can't believe his luck.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Сколько жвачки! Класс!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'So much gum! Cool!' the term ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "класс",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally translates to 'class', and kids shout it for 'cool!' or 'awesome!'. There's one more present.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "А это тебе. Машинка!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And this is for you. A toy car!' the term for toy car, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "машинка",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", is built from ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "Машинка",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", meaning 'car', with a little '-ka' sound at the end that shrinks it into a toy car. Vanya remembers his manners.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Спасибо, папа!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Thanks, Dad!' the Russian word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "спасибо",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the everyday Russian word for 'thank you', historically shortened from 'may God save you'. Then Dad gives an instruction.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "Со всеми поделись поровну, понял?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Share it all equally with everyone, understand?' the term ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "поровну",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'in equal shares', and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "понял",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " at the end asks 'got it?'. Vanya promises.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Понял.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Got it.' Repeating the term ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "понял",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " by itself turns 'did you understand?' straight into 'understood'. Keep an eye on that promise, because Arkady has a question too.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "А можно я пойду посмотрю?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Can I go and have a look?' the expression ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "можно",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " up front asks 'is it allowed?', followed by the action words ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "пойду посмотрю",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " — which literally translates to 'I'll go, I'll look' side by side. An adult in his room says no.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Нельзя? Ладно, пойду учить уроки.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Not allowed? All right, I'll go and do my homework.' the Russian word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Нельзя",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'not allowed', the exact opposite of allowed, and doing homework in Russian is literally ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "учить уроки",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " — which translates to 'to learn lessons'. Now the whole scene again, from the knock at the door.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Привет, папа!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "Привет! Смотри, что у меня есть.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Ого, магнитофон! Японский!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Здравствуйте! Как там в Венгрии?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "Хорошо! Там всё нормально.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Папа, а жвачку ты привёз?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "Жвачку? Денег не хватило.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Ну, папа!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "Ладно, держи. Вот, смотри.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Сколько жвачки! Класс!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "А это тебе. Машинка!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Спасибо, папа!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "father",
   "t": "Со всеми поделись поровну, понял?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Понял.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "А можно я пойду посмотрю?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Нельзя? Ладно, пойду учить уроки.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "That's the first scene, and the show's whole story starts with this one suitcase of presents. Next time we'll find out what happens to that little toy car. See you next time!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Пока!",
   "gap": 0.3
  }
 ],
